    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d674">

                <pb facs="0943" n="819" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg819"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.111 Kalinin, Catherine: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Latvia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Coleman</hi>)<anchor n="32" xml:id="d674-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-04-10T10:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 10,
                                1923—10 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>17. Referring Department’s March 17, 4 p.m. and 31, 5 p.m. to Consulate,<anchor
                        n="33" xml:id="d674-f2"/> authorization visa for Madame Kalinin is canceled.
                    Inform Consuls Riga and Reval at once. Her presence in this country is rendered
                    wholly undesirable by the deep public feeling which has <pb facs="0944" n="820"
                        xml:id="pg820"/> been aroused by the execution of Vicar General Butchkavitch
                    and her exclusion is ordered especially as a protest against the treatment of
                    Butchkavitch and his fellow ecclesiastics.</p>
                <p>Rubenstein also excluded.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d674-f1" n="32" type="source" xml:id="d674-f1-content">
                <p>The information contained in this telegram with respect to the exclusion of Mme.
                    Kalinin was released to the press on Apr. 10.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d674-f2" n="33" xml:id="d674-f2-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
